# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Lua build output. `luac5.4 -p` writes nothing, but a bare `luac5.4` drops
# luac.out into whatever directory it was run from.
*.luac
luac.out

# luacheck's cache. Absolute paths from one machine, useless on another.
.luacheckcache

# Console captures from a test server.
*.log

# Local operator overrides -- never commit a live server's real config
config.local.lua

# Python bytecode from tools/. Machine-specific, and it goes stale the moment
# the script beside it is edited.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Throwaway git worktrees, created for parallel verification runs and removed
# when they finish. Each is a full second checkout of this repository, so
# committing them would add the whole tree twice over and the copies would go
# stale the moment anything here changed.
#
# NO LEADING PATH, DELIBERATELY. The tool that makes them puts them under a dot
# directory whose name is one of the words tools/verify_credit.sh forbids in a
# shipped file, so spelling the full path here would fail that gate on this very
# line. A bare directory name matches it at any depth and says nothing the gate
# objects to. Nothing tracked in this repository is called this.
worktrees/
